{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded","id":772387,"title":"Cowardly dragonblooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T10:15:54-08:00","id":772387,"title":"Cowardly dragonblooded?","content":"A minimum requirement for exaltation is that you are - in some way - heroic...<br /> <br /> but DBs exalt by virtue of their blood, not the fickle and random nature of a heavenly soul-shard.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...so can a non-heroic DB happen? Like, someone with no ambition, who's just a boring nobody? (for NPC purposes...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:20:45-08:00","id":772388,"title":"","content":"If you want it to happen, or need it to happen, and if the book does not explicitely state that it can't happen, it can happen.<br /> Actually, even if the book says that it can't happen, but you want it to happen for story purposes, it can happen.<br /> <br /> So, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:22:01-08:00","id":772390,"title":"","content":"Probably, but I think the likelihood is pretty small. Once you have amazing cosmic powers, you will probably naturally develop goals to leverage those powers and get what you want, even if you had little ambition before. And if you were raised in a DB culture, pretty much everyone of good families of stature is going to have civic responsibilities instilled in them, for the state to better leverage DBs in service of the state when Exaltation happens. <br /> <br /> Also there's nothing fickle or random about Celestial Exaltation. The gods choose. (Unless you're talking about 2e)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:23:54-08:00","id":772393,"title":"","content":"It can, and does happen. But Dragon-Blooded society is a vicious thing, and has no room for the weak. Very frequently, when someone Exalts but proves to be unworthy of the gift that has been given them, their peers or family give them the opportunity to try again in their next incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8899-vayaconqueso","name":"VayaConQueso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:24:24-08:00","id":772394,"title":"","content":"That assumes that blood is the only component of Terrestrial Exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:37:26-08:00","id":772399,"title":"","content":"It would be difficult for an Exalt (any Exalt) to stay a nobody even if they previously were no one notable or of any importance.<br /> <br /> And if the totality of the character can be summed up by &quot;boring nobody&quot; I don't know how they could be in any way interesting or useful for a story. Without just being a blanket statement demeaning the Dragon-Blooded exaltation and its significance or 'standards' in comparison to the other Chosen, that is. Which, in my opinion wouldn't add anything to Exalted or be fair writing for the DBs.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want it to happen and you think it would be conductive to a chronicle or in some way interesting, it's fully your prerogative. I just find &quot;boring nobody&quot; on its own an incredibly poor descriptor for any character.*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Who has any importance as themselves and is not a minor story element lacking identity.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-24-2015, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:41:28-08:00","id":772401,"title":"","content":"You can be a cowardly hero. See Rincewind from Discworld.<br /> <br /> Or the Dragonblooded started out as a Hero, but years of Wyld Hunts and Realm Politics has made them jaded. Now their main goal is to sit around and do nothing for the rest of their life. I'd probably give them high Integrity(?)/Willpower to counteract the effects of Essence Fever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 11-23-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:53:39-08:00","id":772405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded#post772387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minimum requirement for exaltation is that you are - in some way - heroic...<br /> <br /> but DBs exalt by virtue of their blood, not the fickle and random nature of a heavenly soul-shard.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...so can a non-heroic DB happen? Like, someone with no ambition, who's just a boring nobody? (for NPC purposes...)</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of Exalted 'heroic' doesn't necessarily mean brave anymore than it means you're a morally upright citizen or even just vaguely safe to be near. It's using heroic in something like the classic Greek sense, where the hero is an impressive or unusual individual but has one or more tragic flaws to their character. They perform mighty deeds and are larger than life, but they aren't necessarily good or courageous. Odysseus is a hero and he's (depending on your POV) either pragmatic or a coward and a violent jerk on top of it.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of Exaltation, a Dragon Blooded noble who is a cringing coward that prefers to skulk and wheedle and poison his way to greatness is every bit the hero he needs to be. He may not stride forcefully into the audience chamber and hurl the desk of his rival aside with contemptuous might and challenge him to single combat, but the same urge can drive him, the need to crush his foes, see them driven before him and hear the lamentations of their women. He'd just prefer to see it done from a safe distance, ideally by a patsy who has no idea that someone has been pulling the strings.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Exalted, Yzma is just as good as Conan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:00:38-08:00","id":772411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VayaConQueso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772393#post772393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very frequently, when someone Exalts but proves to be unworthy of the gift that has been given them, their peers or family give them the opportunity to try again in their next incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Cite<br /> 2. The DBs are neither this stupid nor this short-sighted as a matter of overarching policy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:12:46-08:00","id":772412,"title":"","content":"I'm sure a lot of DBs Exalt and don't run around doing heric things 24/7. There are probably a lot who just hang out, relax and enjoy their wealth and power and would prefer to run rather than fight if faced with serious opposition. There are probably some boring Dragon Blooded, or Dragon Blooded who were great hero's and are a little more boring these days.<br /> <br /> But then I imagine that is true for many Celestial Exalted as well.<br /> <br /> So I guess it comes down to your definition of &quot;heroic&quot; and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:38:06-08:00","id":772424,"title":"","content":"The obvious: One can be heroic while being cowardly. This is especially true when courage is equated with doing violence.<br /> <br /> The thread question: Given what we know of Dynastic upbringing and that many Dragon-Blooded exalt when they're 12-16, I'd suggest that the average Terrestrial is not 'heroic' when they Exalt. They are kids whose actions and behaviors are strictly controlled by the society they live in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded#post772387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so can a non-heroic DB happen? Like, someone with no ambition, who's just a boring nobody? (for NPC purposes...)</div> </div> </div> </div>A non-heroic DB can happen.<br /> <br /> A DB with no ambition can happen. Given the nature of terrestrial exaltation, a young DB could be all over the place with their desires. Ambition requires focus. An older DB may have achieved what they set out to do and is content with their current situation. Ambition requires you wanting things to change.<br /> <br /> No one is a &quot;boring nobody.&quot; They may seem that way to the PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VayaConQueso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772393#post772393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can, and does happen. But Dragon-Blooded society is a vicious thing, and has no room for the weak. Very frequently, when someone Exalts but proves to be unworthy of the gift that has been given them, their peers or family give them the opportunity to try again in their next incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... no.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded book says that lost eggs who become Immaculate Monks but can't hack it are sometimes killed. Personally, I've found that questionable. Why not bump them to the Legion?<br /> <br /> Dynasts kill their family members but they do so for a wide-range of reasons. While a specific DB might murder their sibling/offspring because they are 'not worthy' of Exaltation, it's probably part of a long-standing personal grudge or or because the person fucked up in a massive way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 11-23-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:03:35-08:00","id":772436,"title":"","content":"I can buy no great ambition. Like a character with no faith in their ability to manage things properly and so is terrified of being given more power and authority because of that concern. So if big situations come up and all the forces available are being mobilized because that's what is needed they'll do fine, but they might choke up at lesser situations because of an abject terror of being standing out to much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:33:54-08:00","id":772460,"title":"","content":"There's a couple positions I've seen on this.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, there's the position that, no, the Dragon blood flowing in their veisn ensures heroism and passion of sorts, and this is fine because sometimes a person is born great and sometimes they become great (that's life for ya), and really it's cooler if all Dragonblooded are heroes. I think this was the Holden position in arguments on this, although I may be mangling his true position, so don't place too much weight on that.<br /> <br /> On the other, there's the position that it's cooler if the Dragonblooded are in a sense capable of being undeserving, or more charitably, capable of being *only* everymen who may not even become better than they are (yet still struggle in a tough world nonetheless), and that the game is better if you can have characters who are like Regent Fokuf (at the extremes) and even then are still Dragonblooded. I think this was the StephenLs position (mangling, weight, etc.).<br /> <br /> I think they both have their charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:36:55-08:00","id":772462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772460#post772460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...that the game is better if you can have characters who are like Regent Fokuf (at the extremes) and even then are still Dragonblooded..</div> </div> </div> </div>Regent Fokuf isn't Dragonblooded (Unless they changed it in Ex3). The fact that he is mortal is why he is Regent. No house would trust a Dragonblooded to sit as Regent without declaring themselves Emperor/Empress. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:21:59-08:00","id":772486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772405#post772405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Exalted, Yzma is just as good as Conan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conan is himself a fairly gray example, too; he skewers a man for making fun of him, chases a nymph across the snows and murders her brothers when they attack him, murders a captain to take his place, steals bundles of stuff, strangles a king to death on his own throne, and otherwise spills an ocean of blood. He saves the day a fair bit, but quite often it's in the course of saving his own ass.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:30:49-08:00","id":772491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772486#post772486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conan is himself a fairly gray example, too; he skewers a man for making fun of him, chases a nymph across the snows and murders her brothers when they attack him, murders a captain to take his place, steals bundles of stuff, strangles a king to death on his own throne, and otherwise spills an ocean of blood. He saves the day a fair bit, but quite often it's in the course of saving his own ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, absolutely. I meant it to be a physical and martial contrast, not a moral one. If we're going to judge based on the actual on-camera actions of the character, Yzma has comitted far fewer crimes and objectionable acts and is arguably the more 'good' of the two by a wide margin. Conan is a thief and a jerk and a not-infrequent casual murderer among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T14:55:09-08:00","id":772548,"title":"","content":"Essence Fever in Third Edition does what Heroic Motivation was supposed to do without the conceptual baggage.<br /> <br /> An Exalt isn't necessarily brave or committed to a herculean task but their essence is a part of them that they're going to want to use. It means the Dragon-Blooded population of the Blessed Isle needs to be carefully controlled because no amount of browbeating from the Scarlet Empress is going to make a policy of &quot;don't use your essence unless you need to&quot; work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T15:31:22-08:00","id":772562,"title":"","content":"Somebody once disparagingly brought up the image of a Dragon Blooded couch potato. I quickly got to the image of a couch potato who is occasionally inconvenienced by their family bribing or pressuring them to use their talents to contribute to some project, if only so that they could get back to their couch without being interrupted. A kind of low-key Mycroft Holmes. I've become rather attached to it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence Fever in Third Edition does what Heroic Motivation was supposed to do without the conceptual baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wouldn't the Essence Fever of the Dragon Blooded be more of the emotional tenor of their Aspect than the grandiosity of the Solars? Either way, I do like it as a quality that the whole enhanced curriculum of the Dragon Blooded youth can be focused on, as well as a thing to get out of the way with one's sabbatical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:51:11-08:00","id":772633,"title":"","content":"Sure they can be unmotivated. They can be generally unmotivated or lounging around between engagements with no driving force behind them other than &quot;have a good time&quot;. Maybe the newly exalted fire aspect ran away from the buck ogre attacking her home village instead of fighting it, maybe the air aspect was willing to just stay married to the sky god that ruled over his people that requires the most handsome youths to be offered to him every year. Maybe the water aspect is perfectly content with spending her days and nights gambling in Nexus, only working long enough to have more money to gamble - the only reason society won't call her a wastrel is because is because some people who have ended up mysteriously drowned. Maybe the wood aspect is perfectly happy being a Guild Factor's concubine with no greater aspirations, the factor is perfectly willing to drape her arm candy with jewelry that matches the flower blossoms that grow in his hair.<br /> <br /> It's just that &quot;Cowardly&quot; isn't the same as &quot;unmotivated&quot;. Being brave is not really a requirement for exaltation. It's not like in 1st or 2nd edition there was a minimum Valor requirement for exaltation. I've always assumed that, considering how much pressure the children of the Realm go through, that most children that survive to exaltation age aren't exactly what you'd call meek<i>.</i> I mean, based on 2e's minimums, every single one of them is at the minimum, educated to a degree most of Creation is not, they are trained in courtly manners and maneuvering and they've been trained to not only defend themselves with blade and bow and fist but to lead others in war. Lookshy's people have even more stringent requirements for their children.<br /> <br /> I find it difficult to believe that anyone who has spent their formative years being pushed so far and so hard to have that particular level of skill when they are 18 years old will be very unmotivated. Their society is set up to produce young men and women who have the same skills as Alexander the Great, even if they aren't backed with the blessing of the elemental dragons. For those that are, they will very likely be swept up by the ambitions of their more motivated peers - an unmotivated exalted dynast is a good 1 dot Ally for a PC Terrestrial.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:30:41-08:00","id":772662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772548#post772548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence Fever in Third Edition does what Heroic Motivation was supposed to do without the conceptual baggage.<br /> <br /> An Exalt isn't necessarily brave or committed to a herculean task but their essence is a part of them that they're going to want to use. It means the Dragon-Blooded population of the Blessed Isle needs to be carefully controlled because no amount of browbeating from the Scarlet Empress is going to make a policy of &quot;don't use your essence unless you need to&quot; work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I was going to say; they may have no great heroic motivation, and just want to live a life of luxury, but when they exalt the power within them demands to be used.<br /> Which is a little dangerous for society, so they keep them in secondary school for training then send them to adventure in the Threshold for a few years with their friends until they've calmed down and come back. Then they're given important responsibilities, high positions, and their family demands they do what they're told. So, they're not going to sit around wasting their time, but not because they're necessarily inherently heroic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:06:02-08:00","id":772683,"title":"","content":"This is a really old and really contentious issue. I suspect that in 3e, Essence Fever will address it to an extent, but there's no perfect answer. It's a matter of which assumptions you want to violate. The problem comes from the combination of the following:<br /> <br /> 1. For a DB with perfect breeding, <i>all</i> their children will Exalt.<br /> 2. To be a candidate for Exaltation, you need to be intrinsically worthy in some way, even before you Exalt.<br /> 3. Therefore, DBs with perfect breeding never produce worthless children. Their genes are just that awesome!<br /> <br /> This leads to unfortunate implications -- it's one thing to say that your genes give you superpowers, but it's another to say that they prevent you from ever producing lazy, cowardly, unworthy heirs. It also discards a major part of the issues with real-world inheritance; when the Immaculate Faith says that DBs are intrinsically worthy to rule because they are superior people (rather than just having more raw power), they're not supposed to be right! The idea of superpowered genetics always carries a risk of unfortunate implications, but this particular issue with the idea of Exalted as &quot;worthy&quot; on some level combined with the idea that, under some circumstances, the children of DBs will always Exalt tends to throw it in stark relief.<br /> <br /> The best solution is probably just to ignore the issue -- to not call attention to it -- because any solution is going to break some key aspect of the setting or involve stating something undesirable. But you can finesse it in a few ways. You can wrestle with the concept of &quot;worthy&quot;. You can say that the process of Exaltation and Essence Fever tend to shock even the most slovenly heir into something more grand. Or you can discard the idea that it was ever true that <i>all</i> children of DBs would Exalt -- turn it into a mythological thing that was never really accurate, a legend of a time when people were better and the world was whole and everyone was in their proper place and so on.<br /> <br /> It still sits on an awkward intersection of nature-vs-nurture, though. Most other Exalted are candidates because they're worthy, so it doesn't come up outside of in-character fretting over whether you were really worthy or why, which can be suitably ambiguous (and Sidereals are centered around Fate, which makes the distinction of nature vs. nurture totally meaningless.) But if you take the various things said about DBs at face value, it makes the statement that &quot;your genes can make you so fundamentally worthy that it is <i>impossible</i> for someone with genes like yours to be unworthy.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can also just roll with that statement, of course, and focus instead on what &quot;worthy&quot; means and whether it really gives the DBs the rights they say it does. But it's awkward.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, 1e had some bits that implied that the &quot;Essence Fever&quot; explanation was the truth and that DBs could be average people pre-Exaltation -- Mnemon, for instance, in one of the Aspect Books, is described as having been average and shy prior to Exaltation and as having changed radically in personality afterwards. But this answer has its own issues.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-23-2015, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:35:27-08:00","id":772695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772486#post772486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conan is himself a fairly gray example, too; he skewers a man for making fun of him, chases a nymph across the snows and murders her brothers when they attack him, murders a captain to take his place, steals bundles of stuff, strangles a king to death on his own throne, and otherwise spills an ocean of blood. He saves the day a fair bit, but quite often it's in the course of saving his own ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to take Conan out of the gray field, but the snow nymph's brothers were pretty much ambushing him to sacrifice his heart and the king was a tyrant who backstabbed him in the first place - the fact Conan was fairly ok with serving said tyrant before the king's envy-fueled betrayal might be much more morally questionable i would guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-12-2016, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:42:09-08:00","id":772700,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that Dragon-Blooded 3rd Edition works over the fantasy eugenics with a drill and a blowtorch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:45:45-08:00","id":772705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772683#post772683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably go with a combination of &quot;Not all children of a DB will Exalt&quot; coupled with &quot;Essence Fever will eventually light enough of a fire under that couch potato's butt to make him do something with his power and act in a manner worthy of Exaltation, which mind you does not necessarily mean goodly heroic deeds, only some manner of achievement&quot;. There's always a Sesus Nagezzer, a gluttonous, obese Dragon-Blooded who decided &quot;Sure, I'll never hold official power, but if I'm the wealthiest Dynast in the world, they'll have to respect me&quot;. So he doesn't couch potate, he directs a vast network of agents throughout Creation to bring wealth constantly flowing into his coffers.<br /> <br /> To put it another way: Terrestrial Exaltation, latent in the blood, either helps all the normal processes - experience, care, and guidance, for example - mold you into the kind of person who will achieve greatness, or will never become active and Exalt you if you would become a useless layabout couch potato with an aversion to any sort of ambition. Attempting to mass-produce children in a DB Baby Factory will produce far more of the latter.<br /> <br /> This would theoretically be why children of Dragon-Blooded are pressured to strive for things and overachieve, with tough schooling and tough love, because if they're spoiled and pampered and never learn to exert themselves or endure a hardship, they won't Exalt no matter how pure the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 11-23-2015, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T22:49:30-08:00","id":772831,"title":"","content":"Squandering your potential isn't the same thing as not being ambitious or not doing things.<br /> <br /> Like, if you want to keep a Dragon-Blood from doing anything of particular note, you might get him into the equivalent of extreme sports or video games or thrill-seeking on the Threshold, but trying to get him to just sit around eating bon-bons and screwing whores all day is probably going to be a hell of a lot of trouble - his nature is to strive, and if the thing he has to strive toward is more bon-bons and whores by gum he is going to go whole hog with it! (Hence where you get the Sesus Nagazzer in the middle of spectacular debauchery going &quot;I am so bored right now&quot; meme)<br /> <br /> Exaltation pushes you toward extremes - if you're a mighty general, you're going to be a <i>spectacular</i> mighty general. If you're a cunning dick, you're going to be a <i>spectacular</i> cunning dick. If you're a fuck-up, you're going to be a <i>spectacular </i>fuck-up. A Dragon-Blooded who is straight-up a failure will approach Carly Fiorina levels of failure. (That's a lot.)<br /> <br /> I would say there are definitely things Dragon-Bloods are lazy as fuck about and in those things you would be flabbergasted with the extent of their laziness. You might even be impressed at the sheer chutzpah of their laziness (like the one story about the navy captain who radioed a new ship heading so the sun would stop being in his eyes at breakfast).<br /> <br /> And if you actually want a Dragon-Blood to sit down and not bother the Empress? I would say that's actually something that happens regularly in the Realm, but the constantly-striving nature of the Exaltation means that controlling the more unsavory parts of the Dynasty is an exercise in continually shoveling food into the mouth of a ravenous Dragon. If you want to keep a DB busy with debauchery they're <i>never</i> going to be satisfied, so you have to throw more delights and more exotic fare at them constantly so they'll stay out of your way. That actually makes the Realm a <i>worse</i> empire than an ordinary bunch of rich decadent elites constantly trying to one-up each other in resource expenditure, because the hunger only gets worse with time.<br /> <br /> Until the Empress disappears, and the Dragon starts eating itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 11-24-2015, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T02:58:34-08:00","id":772892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772695#post772695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to take Conan out of the gray field, but the snow nymph's brothers were pretty much ambushing him to sacrifice his heart...</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the nymph seduced him and led him there intent on murdering him... yet after Conan slew her brothers and she started running again, it was pretty clear she wasn't <i>actually</i> interested in fucking, so his intents of &quot;warming&quot; her were still pretty awful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772695#post772695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and the king was a tyrant who backstabbed him in the first place - the fact Conan was faily ok with serving said tyrant before the king's envy-fueled betrayal might be much more morally questionable i would guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T03:26:32-08:00","id":772904,"title":"","content":"As with all issues of definitions of heroism, analysis of phenotypes, or... basically anything to do with human beings, diversity is your friend. &quot;Hey, is this Exalted person worthy/well bred&quot;? &quot;Well, they're Chosen, so within the boundaries of our limited understanding of how that works... maybe.&quot; &quot;But they have significantly different personality and phenotype traits from certain other Exalted people!&quot; &quot;I suppose the logical conclusion is that there's significant variety to what constitutes worthiness and good breeding, and that it's such a complex, intricate thing that trying to distil it down to some singular, essential traits is an exercise in futility.&quot; &quot;But then, how am I supposed to make a singular label with which to make my club exclusive along lines of personal bias and familiarity?!&quot; &quot;You're heading a right way for a smacked bottom&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can discard the idea that it was ever true that all children of DBs would Exalt -- turn it into a mythological thing that was never really accurate, a legend of a time when people were better and the world was whole and everyone was in their proper place and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I'd be inclined to treat it as what it was; a cloddish invention of Second Edition. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that Dragon-Blooded 3rd Edition works over the fantasy eugenics with a drill and a blowtorch.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly, even considering a form of eugenics that is largely devoid of all the racist overtones of the type &quot;people with southern Italian features are genetically predisposed to criminality, which could either by bred out of them or needs to be kept out of the pure white gene pool with forced sterilisation&quot;, it still doesn't really work, because genetics is too complex and unpredictable. I think the books can have the idea that great-grandparents of the Houses try to arrange matches that they think, based on informed observations, may have better chances of producing Exalted children without needing to give much credibility to that pseudoscience. I even think it's possible to have an idea of the heredity of Exaltation following some genetic principles without becoming too clear cut because of the aforementioned complexity, which includes how much of the genetic code is based on feedback and external processing; we all have gene sequences that never get read or expressed because the conditions are never met, why couldn't that be part of the assumptions of the Dragon Blooded? Still, it may be that certain aspects of the paradigm, including assumptions of the frequency of Exalted children at all, need to be revised significantly; the write-up of the Caul throws a lot into doubt, for the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T03:47:26-08:00","id":772914,"title":"","content":"Being a Hero has nothing to do with courage. Just ask Ciaphas Cain. HERO OF THE IMPERIUM.<br /> Even the biggest coward is capable of doing great things. So, yeah cowards can be Exalted. That makes them no less dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T04:04:19-08:00","id":772925,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the more I think about this &quot;in the blood&quot; thing... not just here, but in any kind of old timey &quot;the daughter of a traitor is probably treacherous as well&quot;... the issue isn't really the assertion of personality traits as arising from genetic predispositions whatsoever, it's just the assumption that these are simplistic, singular things that always occur to the same degree and never have any circumstantial and environmental input. I mean, genetics is already operating at a level far below the factors that produce what we perceive as personality, but to the extent that it does in the form of the guidance and management it provides to the development of our neurology and general anatomy (since at any given time our moods can be affected by, say, input from our musculature or digestive tract, which are themselves dependent on genetically guided construction and management), it's a far more complex and versatile thing than certain Metal Gear Solid-isms. What I'm getting at is that even if one assumed something approximately similar to genetics as being the basis for that Exaltation, it would hardly simplify the issue. Even then... all of the Dragon Blooded from the most reliable group in Creation exist in the same social context, how can one isolate any external factors that may be contributing there? Are any Dynasts going to volunteer to give up children so that you can raise them in complete isolation, such that you can thoroughly determine whether or not the causes of Exaltation are purely internal? How many test subjects would you even need to ensure it was comprehensive? How can you be sure that the isolation itself could not be an environmental factor that provokes certain forms of heroism? There are so many variables...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T04:44:16-08:00","id":772949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772914#post772914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Hero has nothing to do with courage. Just ask Ciaphas Cain. HERO OF THE IMPERIUM.<br /> Even the biggest coward is capable of doing great things. So, yeah cowards can be Exalted. That makes them no less dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the guy i was thinking off, as well as his far less sympathetic inspiration Sir Harry Paget Flashman. FLashman was a bully and a coward who survived one hair raising ordeal after the other, gaining the renown, credit and medals of all the heroes he outlived during the course of his adventures. Perfect example of a Wood Aspect DB with a talent for horses, languages, seduction and running away at speed. Also all the luck, all of it.<br /> The Dynasty reminds me of Victorian Britain a bit, and when populating my setting i tended to steal wholesale from the Flashman books, since Harry met almost everyone who was important IRL during his adventures. Even had a DB Florence Nightingale, in a Creation version of the Crimean War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:49:27-08:00","id":773009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772892#post772892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, the nymph seduced him and led him there intent on murdering him... yet after Conan slew her brothers and she started running again, it was pretty clear she wasn't <i>actually</i> interested in fucking, so his intents of &quot;warming&quot; her were still pretty awful.<br /> <br /> Point, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would be considerably more awful if <b>she were</b> interested, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As an aside, the tale of the old man who recognized Atali for what she was, when he speaks of howling with rage and lust at being too wounded to run after her in his own youth, does leave it in the air that her targets might not be wholly in control of their faculties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:53:36-08:00","id":773068,"title":"","content":"Rape Vs. Feeling Frisky after your brothers died. One is messed up, the other is awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:27:56-08:00","id":773092,"title":"","content":"So, regarding Fantasy Eugenics and the 'heroic motivation' thing leftover from 2e:<br /> <br /> 1) The notion that 'all men are created equal' is patently false in Creation, the simple fact that there's a whole sub-race of magical supersoldiers is just the tip of that particular iceberg.<br /> <br /> 2) The Breeding background pretty well established that the Terrestrial Exaltation is based purely on your genetics. The original Terrestrials were 100% Exalted and it's only interbreeding that stopped it.<br /> <br /> 3) If one were to assume that Terrestrial Exaltation <i>does</i> require the same greatness of personality that Celestials did, it would make sense that those traits were baked into the Terrestrial Exaltation when it was created. You don't want to make a race of easily renewable supersoldiers that have a 50:50 chance or worse of being a lazy insubordinate coward. If you didn't want to run with the assumption that ALL Dragon Blooded are stuck with a personality template it's easy enough to say that the forced personality traits are similarly genetic and NOT 100% tied to the genetic component that triggers the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Personally I've always run it as a genetic crapshoot with no actual spiritual or mental prerequisites. The tendency for DBs to become notable figures of some stripe is accounted for by a combination of how they are raised, slightly better baseline stats than mortals and (especially for Lost Eggs) the fact that if you've suddenly got superpowers there's a tendency to want to use them for <i>something</i> even if it's just cheating at dice, pushing people around and getting laid. Barring some other option that is truly awe-inspiring, that's probably how I'll keep handling it in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:42:10-08:00","id":773096,"title":"","content":"I like having Terrestrial Exaltation being based on some quality of character. It puts added pressure on Dragonblooded parents to raise their children in a way that encourages Exaltation. It gives added weight when you face a Dragonblooded. If they exalted Dragonblooded, you know that they are badass and not some lazy Dynast fucker. They are a product of thousands of years of breeding and a childhood designed to build heroes. I'd still keep some genetic basis for Drama's sake - sometimes no matter now good you are, you don't take the breath of the Dragons. However, if you don't Exalt, society blames you and your parents as failures. Is this fair? No, but life in Creation isn't fair. <br /> <br /> This means that there are less Dragonblooded in the setting, but its a case of quality over quantity. I hope Ex3 makes Dragonblooded as something more than a Joke to Celestial Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T09:23:08-08:00","id":773189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773092#post773092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original Terrestrials were 100% Exalted and it's only interbreeding that stopped it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never had a satisfactory explanation of how the game benefited from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T10:04:16-08:00","id":773219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773189#post773189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had a satisfactory explanation of how the game benefited from this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. It makes sense from a setting/IC perspective, but the only game reason I can come up with for it's inclusion is 'Werewolf had a breeding background too'.<br /> <br /> IC, if you're making a race of superpowered cannon fodder whose whole point is large numbers and easy replenishment, making their <i>personality</i> a criterion for whether or not they are useful would be a pretty stupid design flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:47:09-08:00","id":773476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=772683#post772683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. For a DB with perfect breeding, <i>all</i> their children will Exalt.<br /> 2. To be a candidate for Exaltation, you need to be intrinsically worthy in some way, even before you Exalt.<br /> 3. Therefore, DBs with perfect breeding never produce worthless children. Their genes are just that awesome!<br /> <br /> This leads to unfortunate implications -- it's one thing to say that your genes give you superpowers, but it's another to say that they prevent you from ever producing lazy, cowardly, unworthy heirs. It also discards a major part of the issues with real-world inheritance; when the Immaculate Faith says that DBs are intrinsically worthy to rule because they are superior people (rather than just having more raw power), they're not supposed to be right!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with the Immaculate Faith being based on truth (even if that truth is twisted and obfuscated). It's more interesting for me if it's not entirely BS.<br /> <br /> The idea that Dragonblooded are inherently worthy is not problematic in my mind. (Even if the privileged society they've built is.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:40:00-08:00","id":773537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773092#post773092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I've always run it as a genetic crapshoot with no actual spiritual or mental prerequisites. The tendency for DBs to become notable figures of some stripe is accounted for by a combination of how they are raised, slightly better baseline stats than mortals and (especially for Lost Eggs) the fact that if you've suddenly got superpowers there's a tendency to want to use them for <i>something</i> even if it's just cheating at dice, pushing people around and getting laid. Barring some other option that is truly awe-inspiring, that's probably how I'll keep handling it in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div> Me too, when there's 20,000 of them, plus Essence Fever, that works fine.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T21:01:49-08:00","id":773616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773219#post773219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IC, if you're making a race of superpowered cannon fodder whose whole point is large numbers and easy replenishment, making their <i>personality</i> a criterion for whether or not they are useful would be a pretty stupid design flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>One nice thing about 3e revising the setting set forth in 2e is that assumptions stemming from 2e do not have to be kept. Maybe in 2e the Dragon blooded were designed to be cannon fodder, but in 3e the aspects that differentiate them from the Celestial Exalted can simply be facts; just as Sol could not create Exalted with powers not stemming from his nature of excellence, so could the elemental dragons not stoke the flame of exaltation in the same way as the Incarnae. Their chosen were not created to be disposable cannon fodder, but had the noteworthy advantage of creating a lineage of power, even if lesser power than those of the greatest of Gods, which made their chosen a veritable army of heroes.<br /> <br /> In this model, the terrestrial exaltation is not a spark at a great moment, but kindling laying buried in the soul awaiting the potential for greatness that is required for exaltation, at which point it ignites in power into a raging inferno - the second breath, and a Dragon blooded is born.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hell, we don't even have to keep the same presumptions of 2e. Solar Exaltation is no longer autonomous power packets seeking out people meeting criteria, but the Unconquered Sun personally picking people. Who is to say this doesn't also hold true for lunar, sidereal, and even terrestrial exaltation?<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Additionally, sure, a Dragon blooded can fall into hedonism, just like a solar can, but I think it's crucial to their narrative that they have just as much potential and leaning towards greatness as solars, to stymie efforts to declare them &quot;lesser exalted&quot; or &quot;unworthy&quot;. An individual may be unworthy at a given time in their life due to events unfolding, just like Demetheus drinking himself senseless after splattering Kidale, but that didn't make Demetheus retroactively unworthy, nor does it do so to a child of the Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 11-25-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T00:15:56-08:00","id":773698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773189#post773189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had a satisfactory explanation of how the game benefited from this.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. It means a perfectly normal mortal with no known history of Dragon-Blood can be Chosen as one, which facilitates useful PC and NPC concepts.<br /> 2. It lends a sense of loss, and gives the Dragon-Blooded an end to fear and something to fight for. The slow loss of power as an Age comes to an end is a common theme of inspirational material in Exalted.<br /> 3. It maintains the symmetry that every type of Exalt has fallen, to one degree or another.<br /> 4. You need gradations of purity to facilitate the marriage brokerage aspect of Dynast culture. You can't have gradations of purity without having something defined as truly pure, and other things as impure.<br /> 5. The other obvious alternative, that 100% of DB children Exalt, screws up population math something fierce. The setting is unsustainable if there are 1,000,000 Dynasts.<br /> <br /> As for the OP, I have never personally felt conflicted about the issue. Some heroes are made, and some are born. The Dragon-Blooded are born. Sometimes that power is used, sometimes it's abused, and sometimes it's just plain wasted. As a vehicle to deconstruct power, Exalted invites us to look at the consequences of the various ways it can manifest. Celestial Exalted, Solars and Lunars in particular, are often those folk heroes who have humble beginnings and become much greater. We see they often fall astray. Then we have the Dragon-Blooded, often reared from birth to wield power and govern, and they too often fail.<br /> <br /> I know that view is not popular with people who harbor more romantic notions of the Chosen of the Dragon, but to me, every type of Exalt is equally culpable of being The Problem when they claim to be The Solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T00:37:37-08:00","id":773710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773616#post773616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Exaltation is [...] the Unconquered Sun personally picking people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this being said a lot. What page is this on? (Not saying you're wrong, just curious.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:27:15-08:00","id":773727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773710#post773710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this being said a lot. What page is this on? (Not saying you're wrong, just curious.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a page ref handy, computer is on the fritz, but it may be more commentary from the developers on the forums. I'm very certain at least that they have waxed eloquent in opposition to the 2eism of the autonomous power pellet model in favor of supporting the idea that &quot;The Chosen&quot;is not a cute embellishment or self aggrandizing sobriquiet but a literal statement of fact. Maybe someone else can give page ref or quotation, if I'm lucky. <br /> and on the idea of romanticized Dragon Blooded, I think they have enough ways to be The Problem in their own way without giving fuel to a certain trend of double think I see in the fandom, where any opposition to the Solars must have any legitimacy to their position be whittled away to nothing. I'm not saying you're doing this, mind, only that it is a trend I would rather not have support for. The people who try to claim, for example, that the Grand Prophecy was a lie to disguise greedy ambition on the sidereal part, or who exaggerate the odds the vision of gold would fail so as to paint the sidereals as cowards rather than pragmatists, or attempt to redefine exaltation in such a way as to exclude the Dragon blooded, to make them something Other and Lesser beyond their difference in individual potency. I find it disingenuous and disruptive to earnest discussion, as it leads to memetic issues like &quot;cannon fodder exalted&quot;. A few ways Dragon Blooded can be The Problem without being Fake, Unworthy Exalted:<br /> *) Familial ties that obstruct efforts to be The Solution, either out of genuine loyalty or a desire not to lose influence.<br /> *) Dogmatic rejection of the cooperation required for a solution.<br /> *) Bearing loyalty to, benefiting from, or bowing down to, a power that is a component of the Problem, whether because of exploitative operations (funneling luxuries to the empire at the cost of all the rest of Creation) or aggressive warmongering for increased power and influence (Lookshy hungrily eyeing all it's neighbors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T03:06:29-08:00","id":773782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773698#post773698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other obvious alternative, that 100% of DB children Exalt, screws up population math something fierce. The setting is unsustainable if there are 1,000,000 Dynasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The other obvious answer</i> is that not everyone with the potential to Exalt will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T03:29:21-08:00","id":773790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means a perfectly normal mortal with no known history of Dragon-Blood can be Chosen as one, which facilitates useful PC and NPC concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Couldn't you still get that result with the assumption that even the best Dragon Blooded having had mortal children, and thus mortal descendents? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't have gradations of purity without having something defined as truly pure</div> </div> </div> </div> Well... not really; all you need is one factor that is focused on and thus considered the &quot;pure&quot; quality, since the designation is already an abstract concept. If, hypothetically, gold was considered to be the desirable component of any given mixture, then you could define things according to levels of purity even if 100% gold was actually impossible. It's a lot like how many physical and chemical equations and assumptions are based on a factor derived from a substance or scenario with ideal properties that cannot actually exist; the perfect form doesn't need to be possible, just conceptualised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T05:15:51-08:00","id":773841,"title":"","content":"Levi addressed my main point about truly pure being a vague notion.<br /> <br /> I really can't see the sense of loss. There\u2019s no indication that The Realm or Lookshy know that purebloods were ever a thing and would probably reject such notion as heresy if it was brought to their attention.<br /> <br /> The portrayal of Dragon-Blooded in the game has overwhelmingly been that the ones with lower breeding and mortal parents are more likely to empathise with the powerless. The problem with the Realm has never been its human element, a 100% Exaltation rate would probably look like a boot on mankind\u2019s face forever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T05:19:43-08:00","id":773842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773476#post773476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with the Immaculate Faith being based on truth (even if that truth is twisted and obfuscated). It's more interesting for me if it's not entirely BS.<br /> <br /> The idea that Dragonblooded are inherently worthy is not problematic in my mind. (Even if the privileged society they've built is.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Immaculate Philosophy actually does get the reincarnation cycle somewhat right. Both 1E Abyssals and 1E Sidereals hint that there's a hierarchy to reincarnation from least to greatest (with the Dragon-Blooded at the top) and that Sidereal prayers can push worthy heroes to the &quot;top of the list&quot; for rebirth in the Terrestrial Host. The Immaculate Order only lies about the appropriate behavior to move up that list, that was part of the doctrinal concessions Chejop Kejak made to the Empress after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T07:05:35-08:00","id":773913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773710#post773710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this being said a lot. What page is this on? (Not saying you're wrong, just curious.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It was originally something Hatewheel has been super emphatic about in prior forum posts and such. I don't think there's a page reference in the core book for 3rd Ed that explicitly lays it out, it's just a stated design principle. Frankly, that has always been the way the process is <i>described</i> in the core, the 'heat seeking Exaltation shard' thing only really came up after the fact in 2nd Ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:08:15-08:00","id":773973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773841#post773841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Levi addressed my main point about truly pure being a vague notion.<br /> <br /> I really can't see the sense of loss. There\u2019s no indication that The Realm or Lookshy know that purebloods were ever a thing and would probably reject such notion as heresy if it was brought to their attention.<br /> <br /> The portrayal of Dragon-Blooded in the game has overwhelmingly been that the ones with lower breeding and mortal parents are more likely to empathise with the powerless. The problem with the Realm has never been its human element, a 100% Exaltation rate would probably look like a boot on mankind\u2019s face forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore.<br /> If you want an event to leave the Terrestrial bloodlines as pale shadow of what they once were or in danger of disappearing all together you need look no further than the Great Contagion which is an actual tragedy. The Dilution as-presented in MoEP Dragon-Blooded was caused by them being unable to keep it in their pants and failing to use birth control to such an extent that there's canonically no holdouts of pure Terrestrial Exalted left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:14:52-08:00","id":774142,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think all you really need to get that sense of the Dragon Blooded being fallen and the numbers of well bred families from which new matches could be drawn being rendered down to nothing is as simple as &quot;most of them died&quot;, with just a pinch of &quot;even if it was possible to get their numbers back up again, it would be a disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T04:37:33-08:00","id":777087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=773841#post773841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Levi addressed my main point about truly pure being a vague notion.<br /> <br /> I really can't see the sense of loss. There\u2019s no indication that The Realm or Lookshy know that purebloods were ever a thing and would probably reject such notion as heresy if it was brought to their attention.<br /> <br /> The portrayal of Dragon-Blooded in the game has overwhelmingly been that the ones with lower breeding and mortal parents are more likely to empathise with the powerless. The problem with the Realm has never been its human element, a 100% Exaltation rate would probably look like a boot on mankind\u2019s face forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sense of loss can be felt OC and IC. OC, the person playing the game knows their noble scion of House Mnemon, for all their power and heritage, are but a shadow of what came before. IC, the character has to confront the slow loss of the Dragon's Blood. Their personal political ambitions will be greatly advanced by accepting a mortal spouse, perhaps, but how much will their legacy suffer for it?<br /> <br /> I'm aware my view on it isn't particularly popular. Some people really don't like the notion that the Dragon-Blooded have <i>lost</i> something, and they may not be able to get it back, in the same way everyone <i>lost</i> something with the fall of the First Age. It's a very common element in the kind of fantasy that Exalted pulls from, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T05:52:47-08:00","id":777102,"title":"","content":"The problem with these superior Dragon-Blooded is that they're portrayed in a manner devoid of personal heroism or ambition.<br /> <br /> The most significant contribution they've been noted as making to the Primordial War for example, is 10,000 of them dying to merely slow down one Primordial and the only one of the original Dragon-Blooded with a name is famous for all the babies she had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T05:55:18-08:00","id":777103,"title":"","content":"Personally, I love the idea that the Dragon Blooded have lost <i>something</i>, I'm just very picky about what it is I want them to have lost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Even with the idea that there was never and cannot be a state in which the Exaltation of every child is guaranteed, I would perceive a lot of implications to their losses over time, particularly &quot;there are a lot fewer mortals with significant Terrestrial ancestry, which messes up our propagation&quot; and &quot;there are so few of us and there is so little we still hold that we need to wring every bit of efficiency out of our bloodlines that we can&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, I like the idea that what they've lost is the numbers and the strength of their bloodlines that one could easily not care if they only had a few children and only one or two of them Exalted. When you had vast thousands of others spread across the world doing the same, as well as huge numbers of mortals with good odds of producing Exalted scions, and you're also wielding the fruits of civilization at its height, you can be fairly laid back about things. When you need to desperately make every political and mystical arrangement you can to ensure you have something like five Exalted children, you might be seen to be struggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T11:10:30-08:00","id":777247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/772387-cowardly-dragonblooded?p=777103#post777103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I love the idea that the Dragon Blooded have lost <i>something</i>, I'm just very picky about what it is I want them to have lost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Even with the idea that there was never and cannot be a state in which the Exaltation of every child is guaranteed, I would perceive a lot of implications to their losses over time, particularly &quot;there are a lot fewer mortals with significant Terrestrial ancestry, which messes up our propagation&quot; and &quot;there are so few of us and there is so little we still hold that we need to wring every bit of efficiency out of our bloodlines that we can&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, I like the idea that what they've lost is the numbers and the strength of their bloodlines that one could easily not care if they only had a few children and only one or two of them Exalted. When you had vast thousands of others spread across the world doing the same, as well as huge numbers of mortals with good odds of producing Exalted scions, and you're also wielding the fruits of civilization at its height, you can be fairly laid back about things. When you need to desperately make every political and mystical arrangement you can to ensure you have something like five Exalted children, you might be seen to be struggling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> headcanon accepted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}